# variables-only-restore: pins a variables-only restore.
#
# - The mismatch: the save holds fmt's old code identity. Once fmt is
#   replaced, the runner gives the restore only the Libraries the Host now
#   holds, so a Library the save needs isn't given, and with
#   `mismatch=variables-only` the restore is variables-only, not refused.
# - Discarded and reported in the `restore` line, as a `stop` report's are:
#   the suspended Run shop/r1 in `discarded`, the Delivery d2 still in the
#   mailbox in `dropped`, and shop/r1's pending call in `abandoned`. Nothing
#   is pending, so nothing is settled, and no discarded Run has a `run`.
# - Kept: the Script Variables (`orders` and `last`, as shop/r1's first
#   Segment left them) and the id counters, so the next Delivery is d3 and
#   the next Run shop/r2. The Script is rebuilt from its saved source against
#   the new fmt, so `label` now gives "No. C3".
# The first Pump's Fuel Slice is there only to leave d2 in the mailbox:
# shop/r1's first stretch overruns it at the `ask`, which alone costs more
# than 50, so shop takes no more turns in that Pump.
# Fuel, allocation and state figures are estimates.
# Unblessed: the output lines are written by hand, not by bless.

> add-library fmt
> load shop

> deliver d1 to=shop message=order args=["A1"]
> deliver d2 to=shop message=order args=["B2"]
> pump clock=2026-09-30T10:00:00Z fuel-slice=50
call shop/r1.c1 op=stock.check args=["A1"]
seg shop/r1 start delivery=d1 handler=order clause=1 fuel=141 alloc=56 state=312 end=ask-wait
pumped state=sliced fuel=141 next=2026-09-30T10:00:30Z

> save s1

# Replacing fmt stop-and-reloads shop in this Group. The restore below
# replaces this Group, so this only changes which Libraries the Host holds.
> replace-library fmt carry=yes source="function label sku" & newline & "  return " & quote & "No. " & quote & " & sku" & newline & "end label" & newline
stopped shop reason="reload" discarded=[shop/r1] dropped=[d2] abandoned=[shop/r1.c1]

> restore from=s1 mismatch=variables-only mode=variables-only discarded=[shop/r1] dropped=[d2] abandoned=[shop/r1.c1]

# The ids go on from the save's counters, and `orders` from its saved 1.
> deliver d3 to=shop message=order args=["C3"]
> pump clock=2026-09-30T10:00:01Z
call shop/r2.c1 op=stock.check args=["C3"]
seg shop/r2 start delivery=d3 handler=order clause=1 fuel=141 alloc=56 state=312 end=ask-wait
pumped state=idle fuel=141 next=2026-09-30T10:00:31Z

> vars
vars shop orders=2 last="No. C3"
